\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after 20{} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from 40{} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. The trajectories show model-generated phenotype refinement under each selection policy.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch_adaptive}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. The trajectories show model-generated phenotype refinement under each selection policy}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. The trajectories show model-generated phenotype refinement under each selection policy}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:persona-endpoints}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. The trajectories show model-generated phenotype refinement under each selection policy}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:native-trajectories}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. The trajectories show model-generated phenotype refinement under each selection policy}{figure.1}{}}
